# TOEFL Reading — Day50

## Topic: Plant Adaptation to Dry Environments

Plants living in dry environments have developed various adaptations that help them survive with limited water.

Some plants have thick leaves or stems that store water for long periods. Others have very small leaves, which reduce the amount of water lost through evaporation.

Some desert plants also have extensive root systems. These roots allow them to absorb water from a larger area of soil.

These adaptations demonstrate how plants can respond to environmental conditions and increase their chances of survival.

